": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 77 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Jen Kiggans (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Virginia's 2nd District rematch between Republican incumbent Jen Kiggans and Democrat Elaine Luria is among the most competitive House races of 2026. The district is evenly split politically, and Kiggans holds the usual incumbent advantages, including a modest fundraising lead. But the national climate favors Democrats, and Luria has run an affordability-focused campaign with outside help, including a nearly $1 million Giffords PAC investment.\n\nExpert raters split between Tossup and Democratic-favored ratings, and prediction markets give Luria roughly an 80 percent chance of reclaiming the seat she lost in 2022. The forecast lands at Lean Democratic, with a modest expected margin and wide uncertainty given the absence of recent independent polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7963, "margin": 4.98}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8168, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.777, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7659, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.762, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7557, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.771, "margin": 4.5}]}